SNF(K_Mukai)=[7],
theta=(1/7,5/7),
K theta=(1,3),
order(theta)=7,
b(theta,theta)=2/7 mod 1.
```

# Bottom line

The `Z_7` route is now canonical at the lattice level:

```text
Z_7 = discriminant group of the selected Mukai block.
```

The remaining question is whether the global Fu-Yau/Strominger realization
selects a sector containing this discriminant group as the physical odd CP
quotient.  Once it does, the fixed-sector MTT theorem carries it to the
selected fixed point and the CP labels are its unitary characters.
